 * penumbra_tests/toolvisit/run.php - admin tool page-view logging (2026-09-16).
 *
 * Opening Health, Grants, Notice, Metrics, Calendar, the Repository or a
 * report's Metrics page now writes ACTION='OPEN' against a placeholder report
 * per tool (__HEALTH__, __GRANTS__, ...), the way the landing page always logged
 * __HOME__. The page embeds an HMAC token; penumbra_tool_visit_beacon() posts it
 * from the browser to log_tool_visit.php, whose body is
 * penumbraHandleToolVisitBeacon(). This suite drives that machinery:
 *
 *   - every db_connection.php function involved, LIFTED from the target app by
 *     the tokenizer (never require'd - its top level resolves identity and
 *     opens connections),
 *   - penumbra_tool_visit_beacon() and penumbra_admin_tools() from
 *     penumbra_admin_chrome.php, buildAuthFilter() from get_server_reports.php,
 *   - the wiring on each page and every exclusion site, read as TEXT from the
 *     target files (those are not functions, so they cannot be lifted).
 *
 * Only the database is faked (queryViaOci8 / execClobInsert / logPenumbraAudit),
 * with just enough SQL matching that a changed query changes the answer.
 *
 *   php.exe -n run.php [--app=<app dir>] [--control] [--mutant]
 *
 * --app     defaults to the LIVE webroot; point it at a staging copy before a deploy.
 * --control adds one deliberately false assertion and MUST report FAIL 1.
 * --mutant  removes the token's signature check from the lifted verifier and
 *           MUST turn the forgery assertions red.
 *
 * EXPECTED TAIL: "PASS <n>   FAIL 0". A smaller pass count is a failure too.
 */
